CORE INTENT (LOCKED)
A floating, meditative late-1960s psychedelic folk-rock ballad that feels weightless, mantra-like, and infinite—music that drifts rather than progresses, hypnotic instead of dramatic.

🔒 PRIMARY CONSTRAINTS (HIGH WEIGHT)

Tempo: slow-mid (≈ 70–76 BPM), unhurried, breathing pace
Meter: straight 4/4, but felt loosely—no rigid pulse emphasis
Key Center: D major or close relative, leaning bright but softened by modal color
Harmony: extremely minimal, repeating diatonic progression with almost no harmonic tension; chords feel like they cycle forever rather than resolve

🎸 INSTRUMENTATION CONSTRAINTS
Acoustic Guitar:
gentle, constant strumming or arpeggiated pattern
soft attack, rounded tone, no percussive edge
acts as a floating bed, not a rhythmic driver

Tambura / Drone Texture (CRITICAL):
continuous harmonic drone underneath everything
subtle, sustained, meditative
establishes an Eastern, mantra-like stillness

Bass:
minimal, supportive, rarely walking
often holding or slowly stepping between root tones

Percussion:
very light: brushed drums or restrained kit
no fills that call attention to themselves
groove must feel inevitable, not expressive

🎤 VOCAL CONSTRAINTS (VERY HIGH WEIGHT)

Lead Vocal:
soft, intimate male voice
gentle nasal tone, slightly detached, almost observational
delivery feels calm, resigned, cosmic
phrasing stretches lazily across the bar lines

Backing Vocals:
airy, distant harmonies
mixed low, like voices drifting in space
never dominant, always supportive
Lyric Feel (DO NOT QUOTE):
stream-of-consciousness imagery
repeated mantra-like phrases
words feel secondary to the sound of language

🌌 PRODUCTION & SPATIAL RULES
Reverb: warm, plate-style, moderate decay
Stereo Field: wide but gentle—nothing sharply panned
Dynamics: extremely flat; no big chorus lift
Energy Curve: nearly static from start to finish
Overall Feel: timeless, suspended, dreamlike

🧠 EMOTIONAL TARGET
A sensation of lying on your back, staring at the sky, watching thoughts drift past without reacting to them.

No urgency.
No climax.
No catharsis.

Just endless continuation.

🚫 EXPLICIT AVOIDANCES (NON-NEGOTIABLE)
No dramatic chord changes
No anthem-style chorus
No operatic vocals
No aggressive drums
No modern polish or compression
No obvious build-ups or drops